// The openaimd local client API (design §3, §11).
//
// Every frontend (CLI, TUI, GUI) is a client of this one API, served by the
// daemon over gRPC on a Unix domain socket in its data directory. The socket
// is mode 0600 inside a 0700 directory: anyone who can connect controls the
// identity (ExportBackup hands out the seed under a passphrase the caller
// chooses), so the socket is the security boundary and there is no further
// authentication.
//
// This is a local API, not a wire format. It lives in its own proto package
// (openaim.api.v1) so it can change without touching the wire bodies in
// openaim.v1, and its names never collide with theirs.
//
// Draft: may change freely until the first tagged release.
//
// Conventions:
//   - Buddies are named by a selector string (BuddySelector below).
//   - Identity keys are lowercase unpadded base32 (the invite-link form).
//   - msg_id is the 8-byte synthetic message ID in lowercase hex.
//   - Errors use standard gRPC codes: INVALID_ARGUMENT for bad input,
//     NOT_FOUND for an unknown buddy, ALREADY_EXISTS for a duplicate buddy,
//     FAILED_PRECONDITION when the buddy's state forbids the call.

